batch_outputs:  [["492,000.\n</think>\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **1000** and **492**, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 1000 by each digit of 492, considering their place values:**\n   \n   - **Ones place:**  \n     \\( 1000 \\times 2 = 2000 \\)\n   \n   - **Tens place:**  \n     \\( 1000 \\times 90 = 90,000 \\)\n   \n   - **Hundreds place:**  \n     \\( 1000 \\times 400 = 400,000 \\)\n\n2. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   2000 + 90,000 + 400,000 = 492,000\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{492,\\!000}\n\\]", '']]
