      "text": "39240.\n</think>\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **330** and **118**, we'll break down the multiplication step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 330 by 8 (the ones place digit of 118):**\n   \n   \\[\n   330 \\times 8 = 2640\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 330 by 10 (the tens place digit of 118):**\n   \n   \\[\n   330 \\times 10 = 3300\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 330 by 100 (the hundreds place digit of 118):**\n   \n   \\[\n   330 \\times 100 = 33000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   2640 + 3300 + 33000 = 39240\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{39240}\n\\]",
