      "text": "378,254.\n</think>\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **898** and **423**, we'll break down the multiplication step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 898 by 3 (the ones place digit of 423):**\n   \n   \\[\n   898 \\times 3 = 2694\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 898 by 20 (the tens place digit of 423):**\n   \n   \\[\n   898 \\times 20 = 17960\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 898 by 400 (the hundreds place digit of 423):**\n   \n   \\[\n   898 \\times 400 = 359200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   2694 + 17960 + 359200 = 378254\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{378,\\!254}\n\\]",
