batch_outputs:  [["582,174.\n</think>\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **867** and **672**, we'll use the standard multiplication method, breaking it down into simpler steps.\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 867 by each digit of 672\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place digit (2):**\n   \\[\n   867 \\times 2 = 1,\\!734\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by the tens place digit (7):**\n   \\[\n   867 \\times 70 = 60,\\!690\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place digit (6):**\n   \\[\n   867 \\times 600 = 520,\\!200\n   \\]\n\n### Step 2: Sum all the results\n\n\\[\n1,\\!734 + 60,\\!690 + 520,\\!200 = 582,\\!174\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{582,\\!174}\n\\]", '']]
