      "text": "15282.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of **122** and **126**?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nTo find the product of **122** and **126**, we'll break down the multiplication step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 122 by 6 (the ones place digit of 126):**\n   \n   \\[\n   122 \\times 6 = 732\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 122 by 20 (the tens place digit of 126):**\n   \n   \\[\n   122 \\times 20 = 2440\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 122 by 100 (the hundreds place digit of 126):**\n   \n   \\[\n   122 \\times 100 = 12200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   732 + 2440 + 12200 = 15282\n   \\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe final computed product is \\(\\boxed{15282}\\).",
