batch_outputs:  [["456,106.\n</think>\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **506** and **901**, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 506 by 1 (the ones place digit of 901):**\n   \n   \\[\n   506 \\times 1 = 506\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 506 by 0 (the tens place digit of 901):**\n   \n   \\[\n   506 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 506 by 900 (the hundreds place digit of 901):**\n   \n   \\[\n   506 \\times 900 = 455,\\!400\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   506 + 0 + 455,\\!400 = 456,\\!106\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{456,\\!106}\n\\]", '']]
