      "text": "64,569.\n</think>\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **191** and **339**, we'll use the standard multiplication method, breaking it down into simpler steps.\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 191 by each digit of 339\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place digit (9):**\n   \\[\n   191 \\times 9 = 1719\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by the tens place digit (3), remembering to shift one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   191 \\times 30 = 5730\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place digit (3), shifting two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   191 \\times 300 = 57300\n   \\]\n\n### Step 2: Sum all the results\n\n\\[\n1719 + 5730 + 57300 = 64569\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{64569}\n\\]",
