      "text": "61,732.\n</think>\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **253** and **244**, we'll use the standard multiplication method, breaking it down into simpler steps.\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 253 by each digit of 244\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place digit (4):**\n   \\[\n   253 \\times 4 = 1,\\!012\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by the tens place digit (4), remembering to shift one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   253 \\times 40 = 10,\\!120\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place digit (2), remembering to shift two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   253 \\times 200 = 50,\\!600\n   \\]\n\n### Step 2: Sum all the results\n\n\\[\n1,\\!012 + 10,\\!120 + 50,\\!600 = 61,\\!732\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{61,\\!732}\n\\]",
