      "text": "646,285.\n</think>\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **969** and **665**, we'll use the standard multiplication method, breaking it down into simpler steps.\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 969 by each digit of 665\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place digit (5):**\n   \\[\n   969 \\times 5 = 4,\\!845\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by the tens place digit (6), remembering to shift one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   969 \\times 60 = 58,\\!140\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place digit (6), shifting two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   969 \\times 600 = 581,\\!400\n   \\]\n\n### Step 2: Sum all the results\n\n\\[\n4,\\!845 + 58,\\!140 + 581,\\!400 = 646,\\!285\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{646,\\!285}\n\\]",
