      "index": 0,
      "text": "208,420.\n</think>\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **674** and **310**, we'll break down the multiplication step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 674 by 0 (the ones place digit of 310):**\n   \n   \\[\n   674 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 674 by 10 (the tens place digit of 310):**\n   \n   \\[\n   674 \\times 10 = 6,\\!740\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 674 by 300 (the hundreds place digit of 310):**\n   \n   \\[\n   674 \\times 300 = 202,\\!200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   0 + 6,\\!740 + 202,\\!200 = 208,\\!940\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{208,\\!940}\n\\]",
