      "text": "591,164.\n</think>\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **626** and **954**, we'll use the standard multiplication method, breaking it down into simpler steps.\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 626 by each digit of 954\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place digit (4):**\n   \\[\n   626 \\times 4 = 2504\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by the tens place digit (5), remembering to shift one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   626 \\times 50 = 31300\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place digit (9), shifting two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   626 \\times 900 = 563400\n   \\]\n\n### Step 2: Sum all the results\n\n\\[\n2504 + 31300 + 563400 = 591164\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{591164}\n\\]",
