      "text": "243,484.\n</think>\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **678** and **358**, we'll use the standard multiplication method, breaking it down into simpler steps.\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 678 by each digit of 358\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place digit (8):**\n   \\[\n   678 \\times 8 = 5424\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by the tens place digit (5):**\n   \\[\n   678 \\times 50 = 33900\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place digit (3):**\n   \\[\n   678 \\times 300 = 203400\n   \\]\n\n### Step 2: Sum all the results\n\n\\[\n5424 + 33900 + 203400 = 243424\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{243424}\n\\]",
