batch_outputs:  [["187,262.\n</think>\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **287** and **654**, we'll use the standard multiplication method, breaking it down into simpler steps.\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 287 by each digit of 654\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place digit (4):**\n   \\[\n   287 \\times 4 = 1148\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by the tens place digit (5), remembering to shift one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   287 \\times 50 = 14350\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place digit (6), shifting two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   287 \\times 600 = 172200\n   \\]\n\n### Step 2: Sum all the results\n\n\\[\n1148 + 14350 + 172200 = 187262\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{187262}\n\\]", '']]
