      "text": "91,680.\n</think>\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **405** and **228**, we'll break down the multiplication step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 405 by 8 (the ones place digit of 228):**\n   \n   \\[\n   405 \\times 8 = 3,\\!240\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 405 by 20 (the tens place digit of 228):**\n   \n   \\[\n   405 \\times 20 = 8,\\!100\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 405 by 200 (the hundreds place digit of 228):**\n   \n   \\[\n   405 \\times 200 = 81,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   3,\\!240 + 8,\\!100 + 81,\\!000 = 91,\\!680\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{91,\\!680}\n\\]",
