      "text": "810,144.\n</think>\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **856** and **949**, we'll use the standard multiplication method, breaking it down into simpler steps.\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 856 by each digit of 949\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place digit (9):**\n   \\[\n   856 \\times 9 = 7,\\!704\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by the tens place digit (4), remembering to shift one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   856 \\times 40 = 34,\\!240\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place digit (9), shifting two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   856 \\times 900 = 770,\\!400\n   \\]\n\n### Step 2: Sum all the results\n\n\\[\n7,\\!704 + 34,\\!240 + 770,\\!400 = 810,\\!144\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{810,\\!144}\n\\]",
